{"kind":"finding","id":"F-ledger-career-004-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/LedgerOrchestratorTests.cs","line":1889,"method":"ComputePendingUncommittedStrategyScienceDebit_IgnoresWrongReasonAndWrongSign","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GameActions/LedgerOrchestrator.cs:5934; drop the debit-sign check -> red; drop the StrategyInputReasonKey check at :5927 -> this cell stays green because the wrong-reason fixture (test line 1894) is a 0->60 credit that the sign check already drops","what_it_asserts":"Only the StrategyInput reason, debit-signed event (200->150, 50) is summed; a wrong-reason ScienceChanged credit and a right-reason credit are ignored.","why_weak":"The wrong-reason fixture is itself a credit, so the reason-key predicate is over-determined by the sign predicate: removing the reason filter leaves the result at 50 and the cell green. The name claims both filters, but only the sign filter and the qualifying event are actually pinned.","proposed_action":"Make the wrong-reason fixture a wrong-reason DEBIT (e.g. key=TechResearchScienceReasonKey, valueBefore 100 -> valueAfter 40) and assert it is not summed, so the StrategyInputReasonKey filter at LedgerOrchestrator.cs:5927 is load-bearing.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-ledger-career-004-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/LedgerOrchestratorTests.cs","line":1934,"method":"PendingStrategyScienceDebit_KeepsTheDrawdownGuardFromClampingAnUplift","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GameActions/KspStatePatcher.cs:1177; stub ComputePendingAdjustedRunningScience to return preStrategyRunning -> this cell stays green; only a guard change (KspStatePatcher.cs:3453 Down branch) reds it","what_it_asserts":"ResolveSciencePoolPatch clamps Down to live when the discriminator (raw running 750) sits above live 641.16, and does not clamp when the discriminator is lowered by the pending debit (750 - 108.84).","why_weak":"The pending amount is a hardcoded constant and the fold is re-issued inline (test lines 1952-1956); the production helpers that derive it (LedgerOrchestrator.GetPendingUncommittedStrategyScienceDebit, KspStatePatcher.ComputePendingAdjustedRunningScience) are never called, so deleting or breaking the pending mechanism leaves this cell green while the named clamp+toast symptom returns.","proposed_action":"Derive the discriminator through production (register the recording+event, pending = LedgerOrchestrator.GetPendingUncommittedStrategyScienceDebit(RawRunning, LiveScience), discriminator = RawRunning - pending) or call KspStatePatcher.ComputePendingAdjustedRunningScience; if that duplicates StrategyPrefixHoldbackTests.TheGuardDiscriminatorIsTheBasisMinusTheSamePendingAmount, delete the cell instead.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"LedgerOrchestrator","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/GameActions/LedgerOrchestrator.cs","sut_line":1721,"case_kind":"negative","proposed_name":"NeedsCrewEndStatePopulation_EvaOnlyNoGhostVisual_Admits","sketch":"rec = new Recording { RecordingId = \"rec-eva-only\", VesselName = \"Bill Kerman\", EvaCrewName = \"Bill Kerman\" } with both snapshots null and TerminalStateValue unset; Assert.True(LedgerOrchestrator.NeedsCrewEndStatePopulation(rec)) and Assert.Equal(0, CountLogs for the ghost-visual-only admission line).","guards":"The EvaCrewName conjunct at LedgerOrchestrator.cs:1721: deleting it makes this cell return false. Every existing Eva fixture also carries a GhostVisualSnapshot plus a Destroyed/Recovered terminal, so the ghost-visual arm at :1738 alone admits and the Eva arm is never load-bearing.","risk":"career"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"LedgerOrchestrator","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/GameActions/LedgerOrchestrator.cs","sut_line":7110,"case_kind":"negative","proposed_name":"ResolveStandaloneCommitWindowStartUt_PredecessorIndexMismatch_LeavesSubsetAtOwnStart","sketch":"parent Recording { RecordingId = \"rec-0\", ChainId = \"chain-A\", ChainIndex = 0, ExplicitStartUT = 100.0, ExplicitEndUT = 142.2 } added through RecordingStore.AddCommittedInternal; child { RecordingId = \"rec-1\", ChainId = \"chain-A\", ChainIndex = 2, ParentRecordingId = \"rec-0\", ExplicitStartUT = 142.9, ExplicitEndUT = 200.0 }; pending with a 142.4 capture must not be routed; Assert.Equal(142.9, LedgerOrchestrator.ResolveStandaloneCommitWindowStartUt(child, 142.9)).","guards":"The predecessor.ChainIndex != rec.ChainIndex - 1 conjunct at LedgerOrchestrator.cs:7110: a chain-2 segment must not close a gap against a chain-0 end. Only the matching-index path (LedgerOrchestratorTests.cs:2985) and the null-parent path (:3038) are pinned; dropping this conjunct widens the commit window by a non-predecessor's EndUT. The sibling ChainId conjunct at :7109 is uncovered too (needs a matching-index cross-chain parent).","risk":"career"}
